Z||000000||maninblack||07-18-2001||09:55 PM||||anyone can give me a correct tire size to use on a 16" rims.The tires that cam with the rims is 225/50/16, it looks a little bit odd,cause the tire is too tall for it.it created an outward boudge?<BR>thz in advance||||reg||5
Z||000001||AkursedX||07-18-2001||10:39 PM||||If you go with a 215/50-16, this should cure your problem.  It'll be a little narrower, and the side wall will be a bit shorter.  You could also use a 225/45-16, but I don't know if they make that kind of size.  <P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||07-19-2001||01:52 AM||||Maybe this will help.<BR>Follow the series(top row)down...The first box of sizes is the section width and sidewall...the lower box is the overall diameter.<BR>I made these charts to figure my tire sizes hope this is useful.<P><BR>Joe<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tire.GIF">   <P>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 07-19-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 07-19-2001).]||||reg||1
